Subject: [PATCH] fuzzing: Set up GlobalParams once in LLVMFuzzerInitialize

Since a297ef25 ("oss-fuzz: Make tests faster") the cpp fuzzers create a
GlobalParamsIniter per input so they can call setErrQuiet(true). It is
the first initer, so every input builds and destroys GlobalParams (the
NameToCharCode tables, resident unicode maps, encoding-dir scan): 3.4M +
1.35M fuel, 11-32 % per input. GlobalParams only depends on the
environment, so build it once in LLVMFuzzerInitialize and keep it, and
run the base-14 font search there as well (without fonts installed it
probed 14 fonts x 6 dirs on each input's first font lookup, 1.9M fuel;
fix-setupbasefonts-repeated-search.patch makes later lookups skip it).
document_private's own initer is still never the first one, so the
error callback stays nullptr. What an input can still leave
behind in GlobalParams: CMapCache keeps up to 4 Identity-H/V CMaps keyed
by the font's collection, which a later input may get from the cache
instead of building an equal one; the other caches only fill from
poppler-data files. No related open upstream MRs or issues (gitlab
poppler/poppler "fuzz", "GlobalParams", 2026-11-20; !1973 adds a jbig2
fuzzer only). Drop when upstream initializes GlobalParams once.

diff --git a/cpp/tests/fuzzing/doc_fuzzer.cc b/cpp/tests/fuzzing/doc_fuzzer.cc
index 964ec28..afc2e2f 100644
--- a/cpp/tests/fuzzing/doc_fuzzer.cc
+++ b/cpp/tests/fuzzing/doc_fuzzer.cc
@@ -9,14 +9,22 @@
 const size_t input_size = 32;
 const size_t count = 6;
 
-extern "C" int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *data, size_t size)
+extern "C" int LLVMFuzzerInitialize(int * /*argc*/, char *** /*argv*/)
 {
     initialize_poppler_data_dir();
+    // GlobalParams only depends on the environment: set it up once, not per input
+    static GlobalParamsIniter globalParamsIniter(nullptr);
+    globalParams->setErrQuiet(true);
+    // and look for the base-14 font files now instead of on each input's first font lookup
+    globalParams->setupBaseFonts(nullptr);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+extern "C" int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *data, size_t size)
+{
     if (size < input_size * count) {
         return 0;
     }
-    GlobalParamsIniter globalParamsIniter(nullptr);
-    globalParams->setErrQuiet(true);
     poppler::document *doc = poppler::document::load_from_raw_data((const char *)data, size);
     if (!doc || doc->is_locked()) {
         delete doc;
